==Blog Update==
Following your feedback, we’ll be reverting two specific changes made in this update: the new Tool Leprechaun locations and the movement restrictions placed on Gardeners.

Many of you let us know that the new Leprechaun positions weren’t as helpful as intended, others felt the original placements were already well-placed and part of the rhythm of Farming. Similarly, while locking Gardeners to a small area was meant as a convenience, players felt it took away from the world’s liveliness and charm.

These changes came from a backlogged ticket that had been sitting with us for some time. In hindsight, they should’ve been communicated more clearly and likely polled, as we do with other QoL changes. We’re actively reviewing our internal processes to make sure these kinds of updates are surfaced earlier and given the same visibility and scrutiny as other game changes.

We’ve taken your thoughts on board and will revert both changes with the game update on Wednesday, April 16th. Thanks again for all your feedback, and apologies we missed the mark on this one!

